# Agent memory (SilverKey)

## Layers (use the right one)

| Layer | Where | Use for |
| ----- | ----- | ------- |
| **Repo memory bank** | `.cursor/memory/*.md` (this rule) | Team-visible session focus, progress, stable project notes |
| **Project rules** | `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` | Enforced always/never patterns |
| **AGENTS.md + company rules** | Repo root + `.cursor/rules/shared/*` | Quickstart, company context, RESPA |
| **Cursor Settings → Memories** | Cursor app (account) | Personal preferences across projects |
| **Automations → Memories → Manage** | Cursor cloud per automation | Memory-tool files for scheduled agents |
| **MCP `cursor-memory`** | `.cursor/mcp.json` | Optional `/memo`, `/recall` (local SQLite) |

Do not duplicate long prose from `AGENTS.md` or rules into memory files — link or one-line point.

## When to read `.cursor/memory/`

Before continuing the same workstream (or when explicitly asked for memory context), read:

- `projectbrief.md` — scope and compliance reflex
- `techContext.md` — commands and version pins
- `activeContext.md` — what we are doing now
- `progress.md` — recent shipped work

## When to update

After completing a feature, significant refactor, or architecture change:

1. Update `activeContext.md` (current focus / open questions).
2. Append a dated entry to `progress.md` (what shipped, gates run, follow-ups).
3. If stack or conventions changed, update `techContext.md`.
4. For cross-cutting doc/rule changes, follow `documentation/internal/post-major-change-checklist.md`.

## MCP memory (if enabled)

When `cursor-memory` MCP is enabled in Cursor Settings → MCP:

- Use `/recall` (or tool search) before re-deriving prior decisions.
- Use `/memo` when the user asks to remember something ad hoc (not already in rules).

## Automations

Cursor Automations store memory on Cursor’s servers (not git). **Optimized seeds** live in `.cursor/memory/automations/`:

- **`_core.md`** — prepend to every automation memory file
- **`<persona>.md`** — match automation purpose (see `automations/README.md`)
- **Print for paste:** `./scripts/print-automation-memory.sh <persona>` from repo root

After each automation run, append a **Run log** block per `_core.md` (keep last five).
